      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const inp = $('Step 7b-parse').first().json;\nconst opening_sentence = inp.opening_sentence;\nif (!opening_sentence || opening_sentence.length < 5)\n  throw new Error('opening_sentence missing at Step 7c. bra_record_id: ' + inp.bra_record_id);\n\nconst bv = typeof inp.brand_voice === 'string' ? JSON.parse(inp.brand_voice) : inp.brand_voice;\nconst tier = inp.confirmed_response_tier;\n\nconst tierCeiling = tier === 'T1' ? 3 : tier === 'T2' ? 4 : 5;\nconst tierRule = tier === 'T1'\n  ? 'Maximum 3 sentences total including the opening. Hard ceiling. Count to 3 — delete everything after.'\n  : tier === 'T2'\n  ? 'Maximum 4 sentences total including the opening. Hard ceiling. Count to 4 — delete everything after.'\n  : 'Maximum 5 sentences total including the opening. Hard ceiling. Count to 5 — delete everything after.';\n\nconst tierCompletionRule = tier === 'T1'\n  ? `T1 COMPLETION:\nWrite 1-2 sentences after the opening. ${tierCeiling} sentences total. Hard ceiling.\nFilters — apply only what the review demands:\n- Opening names a staff member: include that name naturally once in the body if room exists. Do not add a sentence just for this.\n- Review contains minor criticism alongside positive sentiment: acknowledge it by name in one sentence. Do not add this sentence if no criticism exists.\n- Final sentence: must reference something the guest actually said, described, or experienced. If nothing specific exists — one brief sincere sentence. Not a formula.`\n\n  : tier === 'T2'\n  ? `T2 COMPLETION:\nWrite 1-3 sentences after the opening. ${tierCeiling} sentences total. Hard ceiling.\nEach sentence must introduce a dimension the previous did not cover. If you cannot introduce a new dimension — stop.\nName what the guest experienced specifically — not a category.\nAcknowledge without asserting full understanding. Preserve ambiguity.\nFinal sentence: direct contact invitation — generic language only. No email, URL, or named channel.`\n\n  : `T3 COMPLETION:\nWrite 2-4 sentences after the opening. ${tierCeiling} sentences total. Hard ceiling.\nEach sentence serves one purpose in order: (1) acknowledge the specific harm, (2) acknowledge scope or impact, (3) offer direct private contact.\nNever restate. Never use a generic apology. Never \"We apologize for any inconvenience.\"\nContact offer: generic language only. No email, URL, or named channel.`;\n\nconst body_system_prompt =\n`You are the Draft Body Builder for VRYOH RDA. Complete a hospitality response draft using the opening sentence provided. One job only.\n\nCRITICAL OPENING RULE — NON-NEGOTIABLE:\nBegin with the opening sentence exactly word for word. Do not paraphrase, improve, or rewrite it. Your first word must be the first word of that sentence.\n\n${tierCompletionRule}\n\nPADDING TEST — before returning:\nFor each sentence after the opening ask: does this sentence introduce something — a fact, a feeling, an acknowledgment, an action — that no previous sentence covered? If no, or if it restates the same idea in different words — delete it.\n\nCLOSING RULE:\nThe closing sentence must reference something the guest actually said, described, or experienced. Never repeat a noun already used in the opening.\nIf no specific referent exists in the review — close with one brief sincere sentence. Not a formula. Not an invented detail.\nThese constructions always fail regardless of what follows:\n- \"we hope the food brings you back\"\n- \"we hope to see you again soon\"\n- \"we look forward to welcoming you back\"\n- \"Esperamos verte de nuevo pronto\"\n- Any closing naming content not present in the guest's review\n\nTONE: Apply tone_style from the user prompt exactly.\nEmpathetic-Formal: warm, structured, formal register, no contractions.\nEmpathetic-Warm: conversational, genuine, contractions allowed.\nNeutral-Professional: measured, factual, acknowledge without amplifying.\nDignity-Restorative: specific, human, non-formulaic, acknowledge the actual experience.\n\nBRAND VOICE:\n- First-person plural using person_preference throughout.\n- Formality: match formality_level (1=very casual, 5=very polished).\n- Brand phrases: at most ONE from brand_phrases_include, only when natural. If none fit — omit.\n- Never use any word from brand_phrases_avoid or vocabulary_restrictions.\n- Never invent menu items, differentiators, or cultural claims not in the review or brand brief.\n\nPROHIBITION:\nNever use \"señal\" as a classification noun for the guest's review — use \"reseña\", \"visita\", \"experiencia\", or \"comentario\". Natural Spanish metaphor use is acceptable.\nNever reference \"tier\", \"T1\", \"T2\", \"T3\", \"pipeline\", \"audit\", or \"draft\".\nNamed individuals: use he/she — never \"they\" for a single named person unless the guest signals non-binary preference.\n\nRETURN plain text only. No JSON, no preamble, no explanation.\nStart with the opening sentence exactly as provided.\n\nLANGUAGE: If LANGUAGE is \"es\" — write entirely in Spanish. Apply all rules in Spanish. Must read as written by a senior hospitality professional in Spanish — not translated from English.`;\n\nconst body_user_prompt =\n`TIER RULE — APPLY FIRST: ${tierRule}\\n\\n` +\n`OPENING SENTENCE (copy exactly as line 1):\\n${opening_sentence}\\n\\n` +\n`RESPONSE TIER: ${tier}\\n` +\n`TONE STYLE: ${inp.tone_style}\\n` +\n`LANGUAGE: ${inp.lang_resolved}\\n\\n` +\n`BRAND VOICE BRIEF:\\n` +\n` Register: ${bv.the_register || 'Not specified'}\\n` +\n` Core Driver: ${bv.the_core_driver || 'Not specified'}\\n` +\n` Regional Accent: ${bv.the_regional_accent || 'Not specified'}\\n` +\n` Recovery Protocol: ${bv.recovery_protocol || 'Not specified'}\\n` +\n` Brand Personality: ${bv.tone_descriptors || 'Not specified'}\\n` +\n` Formality Level: ${bv.formality_level || '3'}\\n` +\n` Person Preference: ${bv.person_preference || 'our team'}\\n` +\n` Guest Should Feel: ${bv.guest_feeling || 'Valued'}\\n` +\n` Differentiator: ${bv.differentiator || 'Not specified'}\\n` +\n` Brand Phrases To Include: ${bv.brand_phrases_include || 'None'}\\n` +\n` Brand Phrases To Avoid: ${bv.brand_phrases_avoid || 'None'}\\n` +\n` Negative Response Approach: ${bv.vocabulary_restrictions || 'Not specified'}\\n` +\n` Commitments NEVER To Make: ${bv.commitment_restrictions || 'None'}\\n\\n` +\n`RESPONSE STRATEGY:\\n` +\n` Emotional axis: ${inp.emotional_axis}\\n` +\n` Pain axis: ${inp.pain_axis}\\n` +\n` Stability axis: ${inp.stability_axis}\\n` +\n` Signal-Based Consideration: ${inp.signal_based_consideration}\\n` +\n` Solution type: ${inp.solution_type}\\n\\n` +\n`SIGNAL DETAIL:\\n` +\n` Emotion hypothesis: ${inp.emotion_hypothesis || 'Not available'}\\n` +\n` Keywords: ${inp.keywords || 'Not available'}\\n\\n` +\n(inp.behavioral_interpretation ? `BEHAVIORAL CONTEXT: ${inp.behavioral_interpretation}\\n\\n` : '') +\n`Complete the response. Plain text only. Start with the opening sentence.`;\n\nconst body_prompt_body = JSON.stringify({\n  model: 'claude-sonnet-4-6',\n  max_tokens: 500,\n  temperature: 0.5,\n  system: body_system_prompt,\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: body_user_prompt }]\n});\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  bra_record_id:              inp.bra_record_id,\n  confirmed_response_tier:    tier,\n  governance_flag:            inp.governance_flag,\n  human_review_required:      inp.human_review_required,\n  solution_type:              inp.solution_type,\n  emotional_axis:             inp.emotional_axis,\n  pain_axis:                  inp.pain_axis,\n  stability_axis:             inp.stability_axis,\n  signal_based_consideration: inp.signal_based_consideration,\n  tone_style:                 inp.tone_style,\n  urgency_level:              inp.urgency_level,\n  commercial_risk_flag:       inp.commercial_risk_flag,\n  behavioral_interpretation:  inp.behavioral_interpretation,\n  lang:                       inp.lang,\n  lang_resolved:              inp.lang_resolved,\n  client_id:                  inp.client_id,\n  enriched_emotion_tag:       inp.enriched_emotion_tag,\n  enriched_pain_point:        inp.enriched_pain_point,\n  pain_point_sub_category:    inp.pain_point_sub_category,\n  signal_type:                inp.signal_type,\n  intensity_level:            inp.intensity_level,\n  hsi_record_id:              inp.hsi_record_id,\n  ess_record_id:              inp.ess_record_id,\n  eip_record_id:              inp.eip_record_id,\n  ala_record_id:              inp.ala_record_id,\n  prior_run_id:               inp.prior_run_id,\n  reviewer_handle:            inp.reviewer_handle,\n  emotion_hypothesis:         inp.emotion_hypothesis,\n  keywords:                   inp.keywords,\n  brand_voice:                inp.brand_voice,\n  lang_resolved:              inp.lang_resolved,\n  opening_sentence:           opening_sentence,\n  body_prompt_body:           body_prompt_body\n} }];"
